      "id": 1,
      "text": "Edgemoor got its name when the original Edgewood community changed it to avoid confusion with a nearby Baltimore town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://delaware.wiki/a/Edgemoor"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village of Edgemoor began in 1871 when the Edgemoor Iron Company built its first industrial facilities there.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edgemoor%2C_Delaware"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Edgemoor lies along the Delaware River corridor, a key artery for Wilmington’s industrial and transportation history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://delaware.wiki/a/Edgemoor"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "First State National Historical Park, near Edgemoor, lets visitors explore colonial events, the Underground Railroad, and early American life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
